        <mxCell id="rI5VgJAClbKEkrU2F_0h-20" parent="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;shapeInside=1;" value="Category Distribution" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="120" x="573" y="360" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rI5VgJAClbKEkrU2F_0h-21" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="This is what we want at the end of this stage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The reason for choosing tournament labels over the maps&#39; User Tags (&quot;aim&quot;, &quot;bursts/streams&quot;, &quot;tech&quot;, ...) is that some mapsets can have multiple tags, each corresponding to a certain difficulty.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This makes it much harder to distinguish the maps we&#39;re dealing with in a mapset, unless I go through them manually and sort them by their tags. Even then, the tags themselves may be inconsistent, since they are labeled by the users. There are many maps that are still unlabeled to this day.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At least there&#39;s a higher chance (still not guaranteed!) that the tournament mapsets stick to one category. It&#39;s the best we have at the moment, without having to go through every map and categorizing them like the osu!Oracle dev somewhat did." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="450" x="408" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
